  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6EBB56">Example <span data-tag="6EBB56">4.3.1.4</span>.</a> Let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be an inner fibration of simplicial sets, and let $e: \Delta ^1 = (\Delta ^0)^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \calC $ be an edge of $\calC $. Then $e$ is an $f$-colimit if and only if it is $f$-coCartesian. </p>
